    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana",
        "uid": "-- Grafana --"
      },
      "description": "Short, factual notes for interpreting the current-process metrics.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Read this first\n\n- **Since core start** means counters from the current `codex-blackbox-core` process lifetime, not all rows saved in SQLite.\n- **Request** means one Codex Responses model turn observed by Envoy/core. If the cards are zero after a restart, no new Codex turn has passed through this core yet.\n- **Tool-call intent** means the model asked for a tool. It does not prove the tool finished.\n- **Tokens** use Codex accounting: cached input is part of input, and total tokens are input plus output.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.1.0",
      "title": "Terminology Guide",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
